WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:10.969
Uh, there is no doubt that what would be best
for my show and shows like the David Pakman

00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:15.599
show and other independent progressive media
shows would be for Donald Trump to be reelected

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:16.880
in November of 2020.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.500
I mean, there's just no denying it whatsoever.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.470
But I'm getting more and more emails from
people with these conspiratorial ideas about

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:29.179
how deep down I actually want Trump to win
because it would be better for my channel.

00:00:29.179 --> 00:00:30.400
Give me a break.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.400
Okay.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.390
This is a show that has been my authentic
and genuine opinion about the world since

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:36.420
day one.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.460
I'm not stupid or blind, right?

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:43.920
Like I understand every progressive show hosts
that I've spoken to understands and agrees

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.300
that we're all doing way better because Donald
Trump was elected over Hillary Clinton.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.110
Political interest has exploded.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:54.430
Donald Trump's outrageous behavior gets people
interested in the news and politics of what's

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:55.430
going on.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:56.430
There's no question about it.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:00.359
I don't know any single serious progressive
hosts who would deny that.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:04.989
But do I want Donald Trump to win even if
some deep down place?

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:11.210
Uh, even if in some deep down place, I recognize
that he's better for my show than Hillary

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:12.210
Clinton.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:17.790
Um, would I want him to defeat Joe Biden or
Bernie Sanders or whoever is the Democratic

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:18.790
nominee?

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:19.790
No, of course not.

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:23.620
And this might come as a shock to you, but
there is actually not a lot of character playing

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:24.860
in left wing media.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:29.770
What I mean by that is on the right you have
all of these people who have had political

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:35.920
awakenings who just happened to be political
awakenings that move them into a lane that

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.549
is very profitable and very well funded on
the right for example.

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:43.159
Uh, and all of a sudden they have a whole
different variety of political views.

00:01:43.159 --> 00:01:47.640
I know that there are or commentators on the
right who were really well funded by certain

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.610
elements of their audience to the point that
there's something called audience capture

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:56.479
going on and they're almost even unable to
articulate their true beliefs because they

00:01:56.479 --> 00:01:58.909
risk jeopardizing the funding that's coming
in.

00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:04.229
I know that that exists, that's not this show
and I don't know any progressive host of the

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:09.130
ones that I personally know that is doing
this sort of character playing calculation

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:13.100
where they say one thing on the show and really
they believe in other one behind the scenes

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:17.120
and in fact to a fault because it's hurt me
in many ways.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:22.450
I've never modulated or modified my views
to appeal to specific slices of the audience

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:26.390
or whatever else, even though it would have
been particularly profitable.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:31.040
So when I tell you that Trump has to go for
the betterment of our country, I mean it,

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:37.470
I'm not playing coy with the reality that
membership and youtube subscribers and podcast

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:42.520
subscribers, the whole thing has gone up way
faster under Donald Trump that under any previous

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:48.230
president, I'll deal with the slower growth
rate that I know will come with the removal

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:50.810
of Donald Trump because it's the right thing.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:51.810
And it's correct.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.530
And I will go even further.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:58.810
I don't even know for sure that it's a drastic
difference at this point in time.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:02:59.810
Yes.

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:03.930
If Hillary had defeated Trump, things would
have been much more boring.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:07.170
Political interest would have been significantly
lower than it is.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:12.980
But now that we've had Trump, I expect that
if Trump loses in 2020, he'll lose his mind.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:18.320
Even with a Democratic president, there will
be, uh, years of crazy stuff going on.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:23.630
And also I believe that Donald Trump's presidency
has had a sort of irreversible change to American

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:27.900
politics that has been caused and things are
going to be wacky and interesting for a long

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:28.900
time.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.870
So I'm also not even really worried that the
growth rate will be significantly lower if

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.410
Donald Trump loses.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:38.500
So accuse me of something reasonable, you
know, telling me my conclusions about taxation

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:43.650
or wrong telling me my foreign policy views
are missing something, but telling me I actually

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:46.930
want Trump to win because he's been good for
the show.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.440
Give me a break, don't waste your time, don't
waste my time with that nonsense.

